L000580	    We use the time-evolving block decimation (TEBD) algorithm with bond dimensions $\chi=550,700$ and system sizes $L=100,80$ for these simulations (all simulations use the python library TeNPy~\cite{tenpy2024}). See supplementary materials for additional numerical evidence of stretched exponential decay in different models~\cite{suppmat}.
